    {
     "tabId": "1b6094dc-1e7b-502e-94a7-d6c94e8c043b",
     "collapsed": false,
     "id": "2c5ba8bc-b1db-57b1-92b1-7631b0b1fe4a",
     "gridsterCoords": {
      "w": 12,
      "x": 1,
      "h": 7,
      "y": 39
     },
     "type": "TextDisplay",
     "title": "How to read this",
     "config": {
      "locationUrl": "",
      "locationFile": "",
      "editorData": "<div style=\"font-family:'Metropolis','Segoe UI',sans-serif;font-size:13px;padding:12px 14px;background:#2b3137;color:#e9edf0;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);border-radius:6px\">\n<h2 style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin:2px 0 10px 0;color:#e9edf0\">ESA write path &mdash; how are the zDOM layer and segment cleaner performing?</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">This screen shows the ESA zDOM layer and the segment cleaner. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">zDOM - cluster</b> and <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">zDOM - per host</b> show the layer's latency and throughput. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Write path internals</b> shows its cache and transaction figures. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Segment cleaning</b> shows the segment cleaner for each host, and <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Back end - per host</b> shows the component manager beneath it.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Reading any column here</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">A blank cell is not a zero.</b> A blank cell means no value was collected for that column in the selected period.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Raw columns are cumulative counts.</b> Where a column has a Raw twin, the Raw column is the cumulative count and the other column is a per-interval rate.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">zDOM - cluster</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN zDOM Cluster</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Lat</span> &mdash; Average read latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Lat</span> &mdash; Average write latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read IOPS</span> &mdash; Read operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write IOPS</span> &mdash; Write operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second read at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second written at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO</span> &mdash; Outstanding IO: operations issued and not yet completed. Latency multiplied by nothing tells you why it is high -- this does. High latency with high outstanding IO is queueing, high latency with low outstanding IO is a slow device.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">zDOM - per host</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN zDOM Per Host</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Lat</span> &mdash; Average read latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Lat</span> &mdash; Average write latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read latency max us</span> &mdash; Worst read latency recorded in the zDOM layer, in microseconds.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write latency max us</span> &mdash; Worst write latency recorded in the zDOM layer, in microseconds.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Unmap latency max us</span> &mdash; Worst unmap latency recorded in the zDOM layer, in microseconds.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read IOPS</span> &mdash; Read operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write IOPS</span> &mdash; Write operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second read at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second written at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO</span> &mdash; Outstanding IO: operations issued and not yet completed. Latency multiplied by nothing tells you why it is high -- this does. High latency with high outstanding IO is queueing, high latency with low outstanding IO is a slow device.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO (write)</span> &mdash; Outstanding write operations.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Write path internals</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN zDOM Write Path</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Disc used % (max)</span> &mdash; Highest disc used percentage in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat avg total op IO</span> &mdash; Average latency of all zDOM operations.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat avg transaction bank</span> &mdash; Average latency of transaction bank operations.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cache ref (rate, total)</span> &mdash; Rate of zDOM cache references, all kinds together.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Bank flush total cache ref (rate)</span> &mdash; Cache references from flushing the transaction bank.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Seg clean context data total cache ref (rate)</span> &mdash; Cache references from segment cleaning.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Transaction prefetch total cache ref (rate)</span> &mdash; Cache references from transaction prefetch.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Transaction lookup cache ref (rate)</span> &mdash; Cache references from transaction lookups.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Transaction (read, write, rate)</span> &mdash; Read-write transaction rate in the zDOM layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Checkpoint worker wakeup ms</span> &mdash; Interval, in milliseconds, at which the checkpoint worker wakes.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Segment cleaning</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Segment Cleaning Per Host</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">IOPS seg cleaner unmap</span> &mdash; Operations per second performed by the segment cleaner.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat avg seg cleaner unmap</span> &mdash; Average segment cleaner unmap latency.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat max seg cleaner unmap</span> &mdash; Worst segment cleaner unmap latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat stddev seg cleaner unmap</span> &mdash; Standard deviation of segment cleaner unmap latency.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Throughput seg cleaner unmap</span> &mdash; Bytes per second moved by the segment cleaner.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Seg clean unmap leaf owner max lat \u00b5s</span> &mdash; Segment cleaner unmap leaf-owner latency: the maximum of the averages, in microseconds.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Unmap IOPS</span> &mdash; Space-reclamation operations per second, including those originated by guests trimming their filesystems.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Unmap Lat</span> &mdash; Average latency of unmap operations.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat max unmap</span> &mdash; Worst unmap latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Unmap count</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of unmap operations.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Back end - per host</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host DOM Component Manager</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Component congestion</span> &mdash; Congestion raised against a single component. Shown beside shared congestion on the same row.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shared congestion</span> &mdash; Shared congestion, as distinct from congestion raised against a single component.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Resync read congestion</span> &mdash; Congestion attributed to resync reads.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Lat</span> &mdash; Average read latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat (max, read)</span> &mdash; Worst read latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Lat</span> &mdash; Average write latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat (max, write)</span> &mdash; Worst write latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat stddev (write)</span> &mdash; Standard deviation of write latency.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read IOPS</span> &mdash; Read operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write IOPS</span> &mdash; Write operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO</span> &mdash; Outstanding IO: operations issued and not yet completed. Latency multiplied by nothing tells you why it is high -- this does. High latency with high outstanding IO is queueing, high latency with low outstanding IO is a slow device.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second read at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second written at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">VM disk queue depth (write)</span> &mdash; Queue depth for virtual disk writes at the component manager.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">VM disk dispatched cost (write)</span> &mdash; Cost of dispatched virtual disk writes, as reported by the component manager.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Namespace dispatched cost (write)</span> &mdash; Cost of dispatched writes to namespace objects, which hold VM configuration files, as reported by the component manager.</p>\n</div>\n",
